cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ORION: Slice Orchestrator Assistant for Multi-Domain 6G Network Slicing"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mayaleh
    given-names: Mahmoud
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahmoudmayaleh/ORION-v1"
abstract: >-
  ORION is an LLM-guided reinforcement-learning system for admission and placement of
  network slices across federated administrative domains. A language model turns an
  operator intent into a structured slice specification and an abstract placement plan;
  a PPO-trained Multi-Domain Orchestrator, KL-regularised toward that plan, decides
  admission and partitions the plan across domains; behaviour-cloned per-domain actors
  place within each domain. The repository contains the system, its test suite, the
  pre-registered experiment protocol, and the experiment entry points.
keywords:
  - network-slicing
  - 6G
  - multi-domain-orchestration
  - reinforcement-learning
  - large-language-models
  - multi-agent-ppo
license: MIT
